{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And Deborah died.</b> What business did Deborah have in the house of Jacob? Rather, since Rebecca said to Jacob, ״וְשָׁלַחְתִּי וּלְקַחְתִּיךָ מִשָּׁם״, she sent Deborah to him in Paddan-aram to bring him out from there, and she died on the way. This I learned from the words of Rabbi Moshe haDarshan." "<b>Below Beit-El.</b> The city sits on a mountain, and she was buried at the foot of the mountain." "<b>Under the oak.</b> On the slope of the plain — for the plain was above, on the slope of the mountain, and the burial below. And the plain of Beit-El they called אַלּוֹן. And the aggadah: he was informed there of a second mourning, for it was told to him about his mother that she had died (Bereshit Rabbah) — and אַלּוֹן in Greek is 'another.' And because they concealed the day of her death, so that people would not curse the womb from which Esau emerged, Scripture too did not publicize it."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {2 "Rashi reads אַלּוֹן as related to Greek ἄλλος ('other'), yielding 'another mourning'; the Hebrew phrase אַחֵר in the manuscript is glossing this Greek word."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:02:11.390613908Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}